  hints: ['For the heading, use an assertion on a locator: <code>to_be_visible()</code> (<code>isVisible()</code> in Kotlin).', 'The address and the title are checked on the <b>page</b>: <code>expect(page).to_have_url(...)</code>, <code>expect(page).to_have_title(...)</code>.', 'You need no waiting code: each assertion keeps checking for up to 5 seconds, which is enough even for the slower server.'],
  solution: { py: 'page.get_by_label("Email").fill("ada@example.com")\npage.get_by_label("Password").fill("secret123")\npage.get_by_role("button", name="Sign in").click()\n\nexpect(page.get_by_role("heading", name="Welcome, Ada")).to_be_visible()\nexpect(page).to_have_url("https://shop.example/account")\nexpect(page).to_have_title("Your account")', kt: 'page.getByLabel("Email").fill("ada@example.com")\npage.getByLabel("Password").fill("secret123")\npage.getByRole(AriaRole.BUTTON, Page.GetByRoleOptions().setName("Sign in")).click()\n\nassertThat(page.getByRole(AriaRole.HEADING, Page.GetByRoleOptions().setName("Welcome, Ada"))).isVisible()\nassertThat(page).hasURL("https://shop.example/account")\nassertThat(page).hasTitle("Your account")' },
